# Angband Module — notices

The Angband Module is distributed under GPL-2.0-only
([LICENSE.GPL2](LICENSE.GPL2)), independent of VectHack's own MIT license.
These notices cover what the Module carries besides the GPL-2.0 code.

## The front end

The Angband front end src/modules/angband/native/main-wasm.c is adapted from
Shelob's main-emscripten.c (ridiculousfish/shelob, branch v3.4.1-emscripten),
which is dual-licensed GPLv2 or the Angband licence; VectHack elects GPLv2.
The adapted ASYNCIFY_REMOVE list in scripts/build/angband-wasm.mk follows
Shelob's recipe.

## Angband — BSD-licensed sources

Most of Angband is under the GPL-2.0-only branch of its dual licence, but a
few of its own files carry BSD-2-clause notices and are compiled into
`public/modules/angband/angband.wasm`. Their binary-form clause requires the
notice to accompany the distribution, so it is reproduced here:

- `message.c`, `message.h` — Copyright (c) 2007 Elly, Andi Sidwell
- `wiz-stats.c` — Copyright (c) 2008 Andi Sidwell
- `z-textblock.c`, `z-textblock.h` — Copyright (c) 2010 Andi Sidwell,
  Copyright (c) 2011 Peter Denison
- `sound.h` — Copyright (c) 2016 Graeme Russ (reaches the build through
  `ui-prefs.c`; no sound back end is linked)

All five carry the identical notice body:

```
